SECTION 2 — TRADING SYSTEM AUDIT
How Signals Are Generated
Signals are generated in two ways:

1. Go Engine (Strategy Registry)
Each of the 120+ registered strategies implements the Strategy interface (engine/internal/strategy/interface.go):

OnTick(tick Tick) []Signal — evaluated on every raw WebSocket trade tick
OnCandle(candle Tick) []Signal — evaluated when a new OHLCV candle closes
Each Signal carries: Symbol, Action (BUY/SELL/HOLD), Confidence (0–1), TargetSize, StopLossPct, TakeProfitPct, AIDecisionID, AIReasoning.

2. Client-Side Mock Engine (client/src/lib/mockTradingEngine.ts)
Signals arrive via API from the research tournament. They carry signal_score, confidence_score, quality_score, mtf_score, and regime classification.

How Trades Are Created

Signal produced by strategy
  → Cooldown filter (15-minute lockout per strategy)
  → AI agent voting (Bull/Bear/Macro/Risk council — all must approve)
  → Risk Engine Validate() — 5 gate checks
  → ExecutionRouter.Route(signal)
     → PaperOMS.Open(req) OR BinanceLive.PlaceOrder(req)
  → Position created with: ID, symbol, side, entryPrice, SL, TP, leverage
  → Fee deducted immediately (0.05% taker)
  → Entry slippage applied (5 bps adverse)
How Positions Are Managed
The PaperOMS (engine/internal/execution/paper_oms.go) maintains a []Position slice (deterministic iteration). On each tick:

Each open position is evaluated: check SL hit, TP hit, max hold (45 min), maintenance margin breach
Breakeven move triggered at 40% progress to TP
Trailing stop triggered at 65% progress to TP (gives back 35% of move)
If margin < 0.5% (maintenance threshold) → LIQUIDATION_RISK close
How Exits Are Handled
Seven exit types are defined:

Exit Reason	Trigger Condition
TP	Price crosses take-profit price
SL	Price crosses stop-loss price
TIME	Position age > 45 minutes
TRAIL	Trailing stop triggered (after 65% to TP)
BREAKEVEN	Protected by BE trigger (40% to TP)
LIQUIDATION_RISK	Margin < 0.5% maintenance
MANUAL	User closes via API
On exit: exit price is calculated with 5 bps adverse slippage, exit fee (0.05%) deducted, PnL recorded, position removed from slice, CloseEvent emitted to analytics.

How TP/SL Works
StopLossPct and TakeProfitPct from the strategy Signal are used to compute absolute prices:
LONG: SL = entryPrice × (1 − slPct), TP = entryPrice × (1 + tpPct)
SHORT: SL = entryPrice × (1 + slPct), TP = entryPrice × (1 − tpPct)
Default R:R must be ≥ 1.5 (enforced client-side in mock engine)
AI agents enforce tight geometry: SL 0.12–0.20%, TP 0.20–0.32%
How Fees Are Calculated
Model: Binance Taker fee = 0.05% per leg
Round-trip: 0.10% (open + close)
Applied in Paper OMS: fee deducted from virtual cash on both open and close
Client mock engine: same fee model (0.05% taker) + 5 bps slippage per side
Fee drag monitoring: fee_pct_of_gross tracked per strategy — DISABLE verdict triggers if fee/gross > 100%
How Funding Is Calculated
NOT VERIFIED FROM SOURCE CODE — No funding rate calculation was found in the Go engine or Python service. The mock trading engine tracks fees and slippage but does not explicitly model perpetual funding rates (8-hourly funding). This is a gap for a BTC perp trading system.

How PnL Is Calculated
Unrealized PnL (LONG): (currentPrice − entryPrice) × positionSizeBTC × leverage − fees

Unrealized PnL (SHORT): (entryPrice − currentPrice) × positionSizeBTC × leverage − fees

Realized PnL: Calculated on close with slippage-adjusted exit price and exit fee deduction.

Account Equity: startingBalance + sum(realizedPnL) + sum(unrealizedPnL)

Expectancy: (winRate × avgWin) − ((1 − winRate) × avgLoss)

