SECTION 18 — FINAL VERDICT
1. What is the biggest weakness?
The AI agent council latency destroys the signal-to-order performance target. Making 3–4 sequential or parallel LLM API calls (OpenAI GPT-4o, Gemini, Groq) on every signal means actual execution latency is 300ms–2000ms. The system states a sub-100ms target but structurally cannot achieve it. For a scalping system trading BTC perpetuals with 0.12% stop losses, a 1.5-second delay is the difference between the intended fill price and a materially worse one. This also means at high signal frequency, the system will queue signals faster than the AI council can process them.

2. What is the biggest strength?
The research tournament + verdict system in researchEdgeScore.ts is genuinely institutional-quality. The combination of: strict promotion thresholds (12 trades, positive expectancy, fee/gross < 50%, PF ≥ 1.1), confidence scaling that never reaches 100%, probe trade exclusion, and per-blocker hypothetical analysis is a sophisticated and correctly designed statistical gatekeeping mechanism. Most retail systems use arbitrary win rate thresholds. This one uses a multi-criteria verdict that correctly models fee drag as a percentage of gross profit — a subtle but critical distinction.

3. Why might mock trading not generate trades?
In order of likelihood:

NO_APPROVED_STRATEGY — The mock engine's NO_APPROVED_STRATEGY gate requires strategies to be in a promotion list. If the research tournament has not promoted any strategies yet (e.g., because none have reached 12 trades with the required metrics), zero signals will be approved regardless of how many arrive.
LOW_SIGNAL_SCORE — The minimum signal score gate (default: 50) may be rejecting signals if the scoring inputs (quality score, multi-timeframe score, threshold adjustment) are producing scores below the threshold.
Cold-start candle gap — Strategies requiring 20+ historical candles (Ichimoku needs 52+, Pivot needs prior-day OHLC) may produce no signals at all for the first hour after engine restart.
EXPOSURE_LIMIT — If the account is already at max open trades (5) from a prior session and positions were not closed, new signals will be blocked.
DAILY_LOSS_LIMIT — If the account hit the 3% daily loss threshold, all new trades are blocked until midnight reset.
REGIME — The regime classifier may be classifying the market as NO_TRADE state, blocking all signals.
AI Council veto — The Risk Arbitrator (GPT-4o) has strict veto conditions including ADX < 15, >3 open positions, and price > 0.4% from VWAP. In ranging markets, this alone could suppress 80%+ of signals.
4. What should be improved first?
Fix the security holes — rotate password123, add authentication to Go engine endpoints. These are day-zero production blockers. Takes 2–4 hours.

5. What should be improved second?
Parallelize the AI agent voting and add decision caching. Run Bull Agent + Bear Agent + Macro Analyst concurrently (Promise.all / goroutine fan-out), then pass results to Risk Arbitrator. Cache decisions keyed on market snapshot hash (5-second granularity). This brings latency from ~1.5s to ~400ms and enables the system to actually trade at the frequency the strategy signals can generate.

6. What should be improved third?
Add compound MongoDB indexes and TTL on the logs collection. Without (strategyId, timestamp, status) compound indexes, every analytics query at 100k+ trades becomes a full collection scan. This is 3–4 hours of work that prevents a future performance cliff. The logs TTL prevents MongoDB Atlas costs from scaling linearly with uptime.

7. What would a hedge fund engineer improve immediately?
"The research promotion criteria are excellent but the live trading risk controls are incomplete."

A hedge fund engineer would immediately:

Add funding rate to the PnL model — a BTC perp position held 45 minutes could pay 2–4 funding periods. This is currently invisible in PnL.
Replace the password123 database credential.
Add position correlation monitoring — opening 5 long BTC futures strategies simultaneously is not diversification, it is 5× concentration.
Implement Kelly Criterion for position sizing — the current fixed TargetSize field in signals means all trades use the same notional regardless of edge quality.
Add an out-of-sample gate to the research engine — currently strategies could overfit to the paper trading period and still get promoted.
